From 2952e9d6b85e7378cb5b1f343bcb2b1594d5e603 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:17:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Draw engine: cross-draw vertex cache

Fetched vertex blocks are kept under a key of the draw's references,
layout and attribute descriptions and resolved ranges, with a 64-bit hash
of the guest bytes in those ranges (merged, so an interleaved buffer is
read once). A lookup re-hashes the ranges and refetches on any change.
Inline draws, draws under 32 vertices and draws with an unresolved source
fetch directly as before. RSX_VERTEX_CACHE=0 disables it;
RSX_VERTEX_CACHE_STATS=1 reports hit rates.

3D Dot Game Heroes: ~460 cacheable draws a frame, ~100% hits after a
scene loads, ~50 MB resident; gameplay 28 -> 29-30 fps (its cap).
---
 libs/video/rsx_draw_engine.c    |  10 +-
 libs/video/rsx_vertex_compact.c | 177 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libs/video/rsx_vertex_compact.h |  10 ++
 3 files changed, 195 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

